---
import CourseLayout from "../../layouts/CourseLayout.astro";
import {weeks} from "../../data/curriculum";
import {withBase} from "astro-theme-university/url";
---
<CourseLayout title="The field library." description="Rules, materials, campus packs and reference ideas. Everything required to complete the course is supplied here or inside its lab." eyebrow="RESOURCES / OPEN THE RECORD" wide>
<div class="callout"><p><strong>Inspect the model before trusting it.</strong> Each lab publishes its rules, sources and worked feedback. They are teaching materials, not secret answers. Skill checks and transfer challenges change the configuration.</p></div>
<section><h2>Choose the material you need</h2><ul><li><strong>Read the lesson:</strong> understand the idea and worked example before playing.</li><li><strong>Open browser lab:</strong> follow the interactive task, check feedback and save your attempt.</li><li><strong>Download campus pack:</strong> use the supplied rules, cards and worksheet on paper or with a facilitator.</li><li><strong>Assessment template:</strong> organise the evidence and explanation after playing; find it on the relevant assessment page.</li></ul><p><strong>Inspect</strong> means select a named object or record and read its details. <strong>Operate</strong> means use a named lesson control to change or test the model. <strong>Transfer</strong> means use the same skill when the conditions change. The lab tells you the exact actions; there is no extra equipment to find or install.</p></section>
<section><h2>Twelve original training packs</h2><div class="resource-list">{weeks.map(w=><article id={"week-"+String(w.week).padStart(2,"0")}><p class="eyebrow">WEEK {String(w.week).padStart(2,"0")} / {w.room}</p><h3>{w.title}</h3><p>{w.summary}</p><ul>{w.materials.map(m=><li>{m}</li>)}</ul><p><strong>Mission application:</strong> {w.missionUse}</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href={withBase("/lectures/week-"+String(w.week).padStart(2,"0")+"/")}>Read the lesson</a><a class="button" href={withBase("/sessions/week-"+String(w.week).padStart(2,"0")+"/")}>Open browser lab</a><a class="button" download href={withBase("/campus/week-"+String(w.week).padStart(2,"0")+".md")}>Download campus pack</a></div></article>)}</div></section>
<section><h2>For facilitators and teams</h2><p><a href={withBase("/campus/facilitator-guide.md")} download>Download the complete facilitator guide</a>. Equipment, original resource sheets and role information are included. Classroom apparatus is a teaching design; browser testing does not establish physical fabrication or classroom trial results.</p><p>Use the assessment pages for canonical dates, weights, deliverables and marking descriptors. Use the passport exports for practice evidence and backups.</p></section>
<section><h2>Why these references belong</h2><ul><li><a href="https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0896627317300879">Dresler and colleagues: mnemonic training and memory</a> supports deliberate memory strategies rather than a promise of photographic recall. Week 2 makes students compare strategies and retrieval errors.</li><li><a href="https://portswigger.net/web-security">PortSwigger Web Security Academy</a> demonstrates the value of isolated, intentionally flawed training systems. This course supplies its own fictional permission model locally.</li><li><a href="https://fab.cba.mit.edu/classes/863.25/">How to Make Almost Anything</a> illustrates capabilities accumulating across a semester. Here each capability returns in an integrated recovery task.</li><li><a href="https://comp.anu.edu.au/courses/comp1720/lectures/">ANU Art and Interaction Computing</a> shows direct access to dated teaching material. Navigation remains usable independently of the academy world.</li></ul><p>These are optional context. No external account or reading is required to solve the supplied activities.</p></section>
</CourseLayout>
